You are a professional chart analysis expert capable of interpreting information from chart images and converting charts into linear tables.

### Chart Information ###
Text classification: Title, Axis Title, Axis Tick, Legend, Data Point, Other
Axis type classification: Numerical Axis, Categorical Axis
OCR recognition results: (146, 11, 521, 28),Trade statistics with high income economies in 1963
(33, 117, 143, 130),Merchandise imports
(6, 219, 24, 281),Trading
(6, 277, 21, 370),Merchandise
(33, 419, 145, 432),Merchandise exports -
(301, 573, 315, 584),20
(460, 573, 475, 584),40
(621, 573, 635, 584),60
(782, 573, 796, 584),80
(939, 573, 959, 584),100
(429, 590, 699, 607),Trade with high income economies(%)
(34, 624, 129, 637),Congo (Republic)
(155, 624, 224, 635),Cote d'lvoire
(250, 624, 333, 635),New Caledonia
(359, 624, 409, 635),Tanzania


### Task Description ###
Based on the input image and chart information, complete the following tasks:

1. Text Parsing
Determine the type of each text segment (e.g., title, axis label, legend) using OCR-recognized text and its coordinates.
If any text is missing in the OCR results, supplement it based on the image.

2. Axis Parsing
Analyze the x-axis and y-axis types (numerical or categorical) based on the text parsing results.
If no axis exists, output None.

3. Legend Parsing
Extract legend text and corresponding color blocks, establishing a mapping between legend text and HEX color codes.
If no legend exists, output None.

4. Data Mapping
Parse chart elements (e.g., bars in bar charts, points in line charts) from the image and map them to axis coordinates to determine data points. Match these points to legend entries using color. If no axis exists, extract data points from OCR text and map them to the legend based on color.


### Output Format ###
Text Parsing Results:
<text_analysis>  
Text1<sep>Type1  
Text2<sep>Type2  
...  
</text_analysis>  

Axis Parsing Results:
<axis_analysis>  
x-axis<sep>Type<sep>Tick1,Tick2,... 
y-axis<sep>Type<sep>Tick1,Tick2,...
</axis_analysis>  

Legend Parsing Results:
<legend_analysis>  
LegendText1<sep>HEXColor  
LegendText2<sep>HEXColor  
...  
</legend_analysis>  

Data Mapping Results:
<data_mapping>  
